6329508 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092709 #edb/ref 1069 "q-42449" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092709 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092709 #edb/ref 1071 "Solve the following system of linear equations by finding the inverse of the coefficient matrix:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-3+z=0 \\\\ 5y-1+3x=2z+1 \\\\ 3z+2x-1=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind  $x+y+z.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092709 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "be9d95c2-a710-5571-987b-8cd6ddd0d0ab" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092709 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's rewrite the system in the correct order:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x+z=3 \\\\ 3x+5y-2z=2 \\\\ 2x-2y+3z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we  write the system in the form $Ax=b$, where $A$ is a $3\\times 3$ matrix and $x$ and $b$ are $3\\times 1$ column vectors. We can do this as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, the solution to $Ax=b$ is given by $x={A}^{-1}b.$ So, we compute ${A}^{-1}$ as follows:\n\n*Step 1:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-0+|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(15-4)+(-6-10) \\\\  & =22-16 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\n*Step 2:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| & |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}11 & 13 & -16 \\\\ 2 & 4 & -4 \\\\ -5 & -7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Step 3:*\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -13 & -16 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 4 \\\\ -5 & 7 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 4:*\n\n$$\n{C}^{T}=[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n*Step 5:*\n\n$$\n{A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T}=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, the solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}11 & -2 & -5 \\\\ -13 & 4 & 7 \\\\ -16 & 4 & 10\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}24 \\\\ -24 \\\\ -30\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $x+y+z=4-4-5=-5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092992 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092993 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092992 #edb/ref 1061 16467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092992 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7bdb49ae-e07e-5e55-b869-25f67ee0ac21" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092992 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186093402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092993 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092993 #edb/ref 1061 16468 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092993 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7e787e4f-33b0-514d-ad4f-569e9dfb525d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092993 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092183 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092994 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092998 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092994 #edb/ref 1061 16469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092994 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "696d1030-ccb5-5376-b23e-62d38e346070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092994 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186092184 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092995 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186092996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186092995 #edb/ref 1061 16484 #edb/ref 1